1
00:00:05,433 --> 00:00:12,467
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,600
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:46,833
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:56,967
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,867 --> 00:01:00,967
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:02,300
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:04,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,967 --> 00:01:07,433
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,033 --> 00:01:11,367
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:17,033
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,333
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:22,000
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,167 --> 00:01:24,867
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:26,167 --> 00:01:28,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:33,467 --> 00:01:35,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,333
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,467 --> 00:01:37,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,167
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:48,367
<i>I don't think we'll get
anything out of this.</i>

24
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,533
<i>We need to think of other ways
to help Gabo.</i>

25
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:53,200
<i>I know a place! We'll surely
make a lot of money there.</i>

26
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,800
<i>What are we going
to be doing there?</i>

27
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,333
<i>Male strippers.
All the rich gays go here.</i>

28
00:01:57,433 --> 00:01:59,500
<i>The long-haired one
is my type!</i>

29
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:03,900
<i>This is Mama Franny.
She's a big-time customer.</i>

30
00:02:04,067 --> 00:02:06,700
<i>Why are you working
in a place like this?</i>

31
00:02:06,867 --> 00:02:09,867
<i>My father needs
to undergo surgery.</i>

32
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:13,400
<i> How much, Gabo?</i>

33
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,900
<i> I'm not that type of person.</i>

34
00:02:15,067 --> 00:02:16,033
[BONES CRUNCHING]

35
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:18,167
[SCREAMING] Ahh!

36
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:19,567
<i> What happened, Gabo?!</i>

37
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,233
<i> I'm being groped by gay men!</i>

38
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,600
<i>And they still want
to get what they want!</i>

39
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,167
It's so hard to help you, Gabo.

40
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:25,267
<i> Did I ask for your help?</i>

41
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:27,067
<i> I can take care of myself!</i>

42
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,400
<i>We've been keeping an eye
on you for a long time now.</i>

43
00:02:32,267 --> 00:02:33,100
<i> What do you need from me?</i>

44
00:02:33,267 --> 00:02:36,600
[GROANS]

45
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:38,000
- [GUNSHOTS]
- Stay down!

46
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,267
<i> Wait, no!</i>

47
00:02:39,433 --> 00:02:41,367
<i>- What do you need from me?
- Gabo, wait!</i>

48
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:49,233
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

49
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,700
Gabo!

50
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,300
Tatang?

51
00:02:54,467 --> 00:03:01,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:03:05,433 --> 00:03:07,800
Let me explain everything.

53
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:11,633
Omeng?

54
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:13,767
Tomas?

55
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:17,100
How did you
get out of jail?

56
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:18,700
That's Uwak.

57
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:22,167
And that's Lawin.

58
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:24,267
They are my messengers.

59
00:03:24,367 --> 00:03:28,067
They monitored your every move.

60
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:30,133
What does this mean?

61
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:31,933
Are they with you?

62
00:03:32,033 --> 00:03:33,000
Gabo.

63
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,300
Out here

64
00:03:35,467 --> 00:03:36,600
we don't call him Tatang.

65
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:38,800
We call him Papang.

66
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:42,133
Just call him Pops.

67
00:03:42,267 --> 00:03:47,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

68
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,600
But how did you
get out of jail?

69
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,633
He's free to leave prison
any time he wants.

70
00:03:50,767 --> 00:03:55,467
To find new members
of our group.

71
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:57,800
The Anino.

72
00:03:58,733 --> 00:04:00,033
I don't understand
what you're saying.

73
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,333
What does this mean?

74
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:12,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

75
00:04:14,867 --> 00:04:16,533
[THUDS]

76
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,133
- [THUDS]
- Why won't it work?

77
00:04:29,667 --> 00:04:31,533
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

78
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:33,733
[DRAWER THUDS]

79
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:41,000
[SIGHS]

80
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,300
Sam.

81
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,633
What's going on?

82
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:46,367
Are you okay?
What's the problem?

83
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,367
- Nothing. Karen?
- Yes?

84
00:04:48,533 --> 00:04:50,367
Is everything set
for the presentation later?

85
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,867
Yes, ma'am, almost complete.

86
00:04:53,033 --> 00:04:54,000
Almost complete?

87
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:55,000
What does that mean?

88
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,133
Is it complete?
Is something missing?

89
00:04:57,233 --> 00:04:58,533
Our report is later!

90
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:00,667
We are waiting
for Borromeo's reports

91
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,333
when they went to Chinatown.

92
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:03,700
Well, where are they?

93
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,867
- They're here!
- Oh great, they're here!

94
00:05:06,967 --> 00:05:08,667
Guys, update?

95
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:12,033
We went to
the jewelry stores in Chinatown.

96
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:13,500
And?

97
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:17,400
There are shops there
that sell jewelry at low prices.

98
00:05:17,533 --> 00:05:19,333
They also sell them
to online sellers.

99
00:05:19,433 --> 00:05:20,567
All of the stores there

100
00:05:20,733 --> 00:05:23,267
are owned by a
man named Mr. Chan.

101
00:05:23,433 --> 00:05:24,933
We also did a background
check on him.

102
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,600
He has been
charged with tax evasion

103
00:05:26,767 --> 00:05:28,067
But he gets away with it.

104
00:05:28,233 --> 00:05:30,100
He seems to have a strong
connections in the government.

105
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,433
Alright, this is what we'll do.

106
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,700
I want a printed report.

107
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:36,900
We need to learn about that.

108
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,800
Where's Rallos?

109
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:40,633
- Rallos? Come here.
- Yes, ma'am!

110
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,733
I need some information
about Mr. Chan.

111
00:05:42,833 --> 00:05:45,700
All of his connections
and his public records.

112
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,100
That needs to be included
in the report later.

113
00:05:47,233 --> 00:05:48,933
- Yes, ma'am, on it.
- Yes, ma'am, on it.

114
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:51,033
- Okay.
- [BULLET] Why are you so tense?

115
00:05:52,567 --> 00:05:54,533
Yeah, why are you panicking?

116
00:05:56,133 --> 00:05:58,067
We shouldn't make a mistake
in our report later.

117
00:05:58,167 --> 00:06:00,200
Someone will be sitting in
on our briefing.

118
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,300
- Who?
- Who?

119
00:06:01,467 --> 00:06:05,100
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:06:05,267 --> 00:06:08,967
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

121
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,100
Hi, guys!

122
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:28,300
[PIA] Well?

123
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:30,133
It's like you've seen a ghost.

124
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,267
I'm right here.

125
00:06:33,367 --> 00:06:34,800
No one even greeted me.

126
00:06:37,533 --> 00:06:40,133
Um...
Good evening, Ma'am Pia.

127
00:06:40,267 --> 00:06:47,100
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

128
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,867
[CLEARS THROAT]

129
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,800
The briefing is in 10 minutes.
Are you ready?

130
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:55,667
Yes.

131
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:58,933
I really hope you are.

132
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:01,167
Tick.

133
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,000
Tock.

134
00:07:03,167 --> 00:07:04,800
Tick.

135
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:06,000
Tock.

136
00:07:06,167 --> 00:07:13,000
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,700
Oh no.

138
00:07:25,833 --> 00:07:27,567
She became a clock.

139
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,567
- [CLAPS]
- Hurry up!

140
00:07:31,733 --> 00:07:33,633
- Yes, Ma'am.
- Let's go.

141
00:07:40,667 --> 00:07:41,533
We can do it,

142
00:07:41,667 --> 00:07:43,000
Tick tock.

143
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:44,633
- [CLAPS]
- Let's go. [CHUCKLES]

144
00:07:44,733 --> 00:07:51,833
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:08:06,967 --> 00:08:07,533
[PIA] Sir!

146
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,533
Oh, Pia.

147
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:11,500
What's up?

148
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,667
Are you ready for...

149
00:08:13,767 --> 00:08:16,067
the briefing of...

150
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:17,867
your favorite agent?

151
00:08:19,067 --> 00:08:20,900
I just hope she doesn't
embarrass you.

152
00:08:22,467 --> 00:08:25,233
She knows that you'll
be there for the briefing.

153
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:28,200
Sam is detail-oriented.

154
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:31,400
She'll never embarrass me
with how she handles the case.

155
00:08:31,567 --> 00:08:32,800
Well, I do hope... [SCOFFS]

156
00:08:32,933 --> 00:08:36,367
that you made the right choice
to trust her.

157
00:08:36,467 --> 00:08:38,900
[BREATHES SHARPLY]

158
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,733
Sebastian's there anyway.

159
00:08:41,833 --> 00:08:45,200
In my eyes, he's miles better
compared to Sam.

160
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:47,067
There's no need to compare.

161
00:08:48,767 --> 00:08:51,367
All of my agents are excellent.

162
00:08:51,467 --> 00:08:52,733
We'll see about that.

163
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:57,700
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:08:57,833 --> 00:08:58,933
[DOOR OPENS]

165
00:09:00,633 --> 00:09:03,100
[DOOR CREAKING CLOSE]

166
00:09:05,033 --> 00:09:08,500
The demolition they did
at Ginintuang Lupa earlier

167
00:09:08,633 --> 00:09:10,267
was horrible.

168
00:09:10,433 --> 00:09:12,567
They treated those people
as if they're animals.

169
00:09:12,667 --> 00:09:13,767
Just to get them to leave.

170
00:09:13,933 --> 00:09:16,267
My friend, take it easy!

171
00:09:16,367 --> 00:09:18,400
You're way too affected by it.

172
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:22,633
We went there to cover
all the events that happened.

173
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,600
Wait, do you live there?

174
00:09:24,767 --> 00:09:27,267
Do you have relatives
who live there?

175
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,433
[THUDS, SIGHS]

176
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:30,133
I don't, Oli.

177
00:09:30,233 --> 00:09:34,600
But of course, I can sympathize
with them.

178
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,433
They don't have much
on them to begin with.

179
00:09:36,533 --> 00:09:38,467
- [THUDS]
- Well, Salvador,

180
00:09:38,567 --> 00:09:40,333
it's all part of the job.

181
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,767
Keep your feelings separated
from the issue!

182
00:09:42,867 --> 00:09:47,700
You shouldn't be too invested
with everything!

183
00:09:47,833 --> 00:09:49,367
Especially with your job.

184
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
[EXHALES DEEPLY] I don't know...

185
00:09:53,167 --> 00:09:54,300
Salvador.

186
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,000
Sir Arnel is calling for you.

187
00:09:57,167 --> 00:09:58,600
Oh? See?

188
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:02,000
Our executive producer
is calling for us.

189
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,233
Why? For what?

190
00:10:03,367 --> 00:10:06,167
I'm sure that it's because
of those feelings you have.

191
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,867
Feelings!

192
00:10:09,033 --> 00:10:10,800
- [THUDS]
- [SALVADOR] Let's go.

193
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:13,000
- You yap way too much.
- [OLI SIGHS]

194
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,400
- [SALVADOR, INAUDIBLE]
- Oh, man.

195
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:17,000
- [OLI] Boss?
- [SALVADOR] Boss!

196
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:19,167
[OLI] Uh, they said you
wanted to talk to us?

197
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:21,633
Take a seat.

198
00:10:21,733 --> 00:10:24,000
Oh, thank you, boss.

199
00:10:24,167 --> 00:10:27,167
Oh, man. [CLEARS THROAT, CLAPS]

200
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:29,033
How was the coverage

201
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,467
of the Ginintuang Lupa
demolition for you two?

202
00:10:31,567 --> 00:10:33,700
It was awful, boss, truly.

203
00:10:33,867 --> 00:10:36,367
Everyone was fighting.
You'd think there's a war.

204
00:10:36,567 --> 00:10:38,700
We even got caught in the middle
with the police.

205
00:10:38,867 --> 00:10:40,000
[OLI] Boss! [LAUGHS]

206
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:42,933
Salvador and I did our big one
on this coverage!

207
00:10:43,067 --> 00:10:46,267
- The best! [LAUGHING]
- [CLAPS]

208
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:47,367
[CLATTERS]

209
00:10:47,467 --> 00:10:48,500
That's it?!

210
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:51,067
No executive producer
would be happy hearing that!

211
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:54,367
There are a lot of reporters
who cover

212
00:10:54,467 --> 00:10:56,200
the eruption of a volcano!

213
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:58,867
Some of them even almost get
washed away by a tsunami!

214
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:02,700
And this is your report?

215
00:11:02,867 --> 00:11:03,700
Are you proud of it?

216
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,867
Boss, listen.

217
00:11:05,033 --> 00:11:06,667
We covered everything.

218
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:08,867
What happened was very real.

219
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,900
You covered it indeed

220
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:15,233
but did anyone bother watching
your lousy report?

221
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:19,133
You've been in the industry
for years, Salvador!

222
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:21,567
I've been watching you
ever since I was in college!

223
00:11:21,667 --> 00:11:24,600
You know what kind of product
you should be creating!

224
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:28,400
What we need
is controversial news!

225
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:29,933
Sensational!

226
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:33,933
Something that feels as if
you're watching a melodrama!

227
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:35,733
Wh-- what do you want, boss?

228
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:38,567
For me to distort the facts?

229
00:11:38,667 --> 00:11:39,800
I'm not that kind
of person, boss.

230
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:42,100
You're an employee
of the company!

231
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:45,000
Your responsibility is not
to the truth

232
00:11:45,133 --> 00:11:46,767
but to the ratings and income

233
00:11:46,933 --> 00:11:48,967
of the company
that's paying you.

234
00:11:49,133 --> 00:11:50,933
Make a follow-up report on this!

235
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,567
A story that's worthwhile!

236
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:55,567
Roger, boss.

237
00:11:55,667 --> 00:11:57,800
Thank you. Let's go, Oli.

238
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,500
You're worthwhile, Oli.

239
00:12:00,833 --> 00:12:02,167
[SALVADOR] Telebalita viewers,

240
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,333
<i>we're currently here
at Ginintuang Lupa</i>

241
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:08,233
<i>where the police has begun
their demolition operation.</i>

242
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:11,967
<i>The supposed peaceful
and orderly demolition</i>

243
00:12:12,133 --> 00:12:14,800
<i>turned into a massive chaos
due to someone firing a gun.</i>

244
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:17,667
Sir.

245
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:18,967
[SMACKS]

246
00:12:19,133 --> 00:12:21,000
We're the bad guys again.

247
00:12:21,167 --> 00:12:22,700
They should be thankful
we didn't fire back

248
00:12:22,833 --> 00:12:23,967
at those bastards.

249
00:12:24,133 --> 00:12:26,667
You should get used
to them always antagonizing us.

250
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:28,267
What's important...

251
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:31,300
is that the demolition
didn't push through.

252
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,533
Sir.

253
00:12:32,667 --> 00:12:34,633
We will lose a lot

254
00:12:34,733 --> 00:12:37,200
if we lose Ginintuang Lupa.

255
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:41,200
Why do you have to listen
to General Jacinto anyway?

256
00:12:41,333 --> 00:12:43,967
I'm just trying to give back
to him

257
00:12:44,133 --> 00:12:45,333
because if it weren't for him,

258
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,367
I wouldn't be
in this position now.

259
00:12:49,367 --> 00:12:50,667
[SIGHS]

260
00:12:50,833 --> 00:12:54,000
Sir, if you were to choose...

261
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:56,500
General Jacinto's words
or Ginintuang Lupa?

262
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,033
Which will you choose?

263
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:02,000
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:13:02,167 --> 00:13:05,967
Next time, I will choose myself.

265
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:10,733
And I am catering to everyone
who needs me, am I not?

266
00:13:10,867 --> 00:13:14,033
But if those two
were to collide...

267
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,500
and I had to let go
of the other...

268
00:13:19,033 --> 00:13:21,333
I'll choose the one...

269
00:13:21,533 --> 00:13:24,367
that'll be beneficial to me
in the long run.

270
00:13:26,633 --> 00:13:28,033
[DJANGO] Pa.

271
00:13:28,133 --> 00:13:30,533
That Umali...

272
00:13:30,633 --> 00:13:33,267
he didn't stick to our deal.

273
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:36,067
He even supports the demolition
of Ginintuang Lupa!

274
00:13:36,233 --> 00:13:40,000
As if they don't benefit
from using us.

275
00:13:41,033 --> 00:13:43,433
You know how those cops are.

276
00:13:43,567 --> 00:13:46,500
If the won't gain anything
from it, they don't care.

277
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,233
Why?

278
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:50,233
We have something
to throw at them anyway!

279
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:51,533
Money!

280
00:13:51,633 --> 00:13:54,400
If you think about it, they're
benefiting off of us a lot.

281
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:57,067
[PAQUITO] You know,

282
00:13:57,167 --> 00:14:00,067
our deal with the police
is crystal clear.

283
00:14:00,233 --> 00:14:02,867
They will protect us

284
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:05,100
and we'll pay them.

285
00:14:06,833 --> 00:14:09,267
To what extent will they
protect us?

286
00:14:09,433 --> 00:14:10,733
With mere words?

287
00:14:11,933 --> 00:14:12,967
You know what? I think,

288
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:14,900
once they see an opening,

289
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,400
they'll betray us for sure.

290
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:19,900
[PAQUITO] I'd like
to see them try!

291
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,100
Don't they know that...

292
00:14:22,267 --> 00:14:25,767
people in Ginintuang Lupa
are ruthless?

293
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:27,033
Try me.

294
00:14:27,133 --> 00:14:28,900
They don't know what's coming.

295
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,300
Pa...

296
00:14:30,467 --> 00:14:33,133
I know we have an arrangement
with the police,

297
00:14:34,267 --> 00:14:37,167
but I hope they don't fool us.

298
00:14:38,767 --> 00:14:41,600
Because no one is more clever
than us criminals!

299
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:42,800
Even if they're the police,

300
00:14:42,967 --> 00:14:44,333
[GUN COCKS]

301
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:47,000
I won't let them get away.

302
00:14:47,133 --> 00:14:48,633
[LAUGHS MANIACALLY]

303
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,567
[THUDS]

304
00:14:50,667 --> 00:14:52,433
He's your son, no doubt.

305
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:53,567
[THUDS]

306
00:14:53,667 --> 00:14:57,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

307
00:14:57,333 --> 00:15:00,267
[PAPANG] Our country
is too chaotic, son.

308
00:15:03,467 --> 00:15:06,533
The chaos around is rampant.

309
00:15:10,867 --> 00:15:12,533
Even our government...

310
00:15:14,067 --> 00:15:16,767
can't contain the surge
of criminals anymore.

311
00:15:16,867 --> 00:15:18,133
And sometimes,

312
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:20,500
the criminals
are already working

313
00:15:20,667 --> 00:15:22,333
with those in power.

314
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,867
Even the police.

315
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,133
They can't do anything about it.

316
00:15:25,233 --> 00:15:27,200
That's why Anino is here.

317
00:15:29,233 --> 00:15:33,767
To help clean our country.

318
00:15:33,867 --> 00:15:40,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

319
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:46,000
We need someone
who is wholehearted.

320
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:51,533
A good fighter, fearless,
and someone integrity.

321
00:15:53,567 --> 00:15:55,867
We need you, Gabo.

322
00:15:56,033 --> 00:16:03,033
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:16:08,633 --> 00:16:10,233
We've been watching you
for a long time, Gabo.

324
00:16:11,467 --> 00:16:13,167
[OMENG] And Macaraig?

325
00:16:13,267 --> 00:16:14,567
He's one of us.

326
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:18,233
He's in charge of screening
potential members.

327
00:16:18,367 --> 00:16:25,033
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:16:26,367 --> 00:16:29,167
<i>Pops, how long are you
planning to stay inside?</i>

329
00:16:29,267 --> 00:16:31,067
<i> It depends.</i>

330
00:16:31,233 --> 00:16:35,267
<i>Until I find someone who has
potential to be part of Anino.</i>

331
00:16:35,433 --> 00:16:39,167
Once you do, tell us right away,
<i> so we can help seize him up.</i>

332
00:16:40,467 --> 00:16:41,567
<i> Pops.</i>

333
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:48,433
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

334
00:16:50,633 --> 00:16:52,600
[ECHOING THWACK, BLOWS LAND]

335
00:16:52,733 --> 00:16:55,733
[PAPANG]<i> I recruited
</i> the wrong guy for Anino.

336
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:57,933
<i>Now, I'm looking
for his replacement.</i>

337
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,767
<i>There are many thugs here
who are willing to kill</i>

338
00:17:01,933 --> 00:17:04,533
<i> and can take on your orders.</i>

339
00:17:05,433 --> 00:17:08,233
<i>Yes, there are a lot
of brave souls here,</i>

340
00:17:08,333 --> 00:17:12,267
<i>but only a few of them have
the heart of a true warrior.</i>

341
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,300
[THWACKS]

342
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,100
[THUDS]

343
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:18,733
[THUDS]

344
00:17:18,833 --> 00:17:25,833
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

345
00:17:33,667 --> 00:17:34,600
[THUDS]

346
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:35,933
[THWACKS]

347
00:17:37,767 --> 00:17:39,400
[BLOWS THWACKING]

348
00:17:55,233 --> 00:18:02,000
[WHOOSHING]

349
00:18:04,633 --> 00:18:07,333
- [METAL GRILLS CLANG]
- [BLOWS LAND]

350
00:18:09,133 --> 00:18:11,133
<i>- Tatang, Pedro's here.
- Hey.</i>

351
00:18:11,233 --> 00:18:12,633
[PAPANG] Come in.

352
00:18:12,733 --> 00:18:14,033
[PEDRO] Tatang, good evening.

353
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,700
<i> Have a seat.</i>

354
00:18:17,033 --> 00:18:21,033
Tomorrow, I want you to stab me
<i> at the basketball court.</i>

355
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:23,000
<i> What are you planning, Tatang?</i>

356
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:25,200
<i> I just want to test someone.</i>

357
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,300
<i> Gabo.</i>

358
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:31,367
- [STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

359
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:32,833
[PAPANG] Wait for my signal.

360
00:18:32,933 --> 00:18:39,400
[INMATES SHOUTING]

361
00:18:39,567 --> 00:18:46,300
[MUSIC BUILDS]

362
00:18:47,367 --> 00:18:50,333
[PUNCHES LANDING]

363
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:55,867
[INMATE] Hey!

364
00:18:56,067 --> 00:19:02,267
- [INMATES SHOUTING]
- [BLOWS, KICKS LANDING]

365
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:04,733
[FLESH RIPS]

366
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,567
[KICKS, BLOWS LANDING]

367
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:08,600
[OMENG] Gabo!

368
00:19:08,767 --> 00:19:09,900
<i> Tatang got stabbed!</i>

369
00:19:10,033 --> 00:19:10,900
<i> Get him out of here!</i>

370
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:12,500
<i> - Hurry!
</i>- [PAPANG GRUNTS]

371
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:19,500
- [INMATES CONTINUE SHOUTING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

372
00:19:23,967 --> 00:19:25,267
[ECHOING BLOW]

373
00:19:25,433 --> 00:19:29,400
[PAPANG] We put you
through many tests, Gabo.

374
00:19:30,267 --> 00:19:31,767
[GABO]<i> What's this?!
</i> What are you doing to me?

375
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:33,633
[WARDEN] I heard you're tough.

376
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,400
<i>- Let's see about that!
- [GABO GRUNTS]</i>

377
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:40,700
[PAPANG] To make sure you're
the perfect person for the job.

378
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:41,900
[WARDEN] Dunk him!

379
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,567
- [GRUNTS]
- [LOUD SPLASH]

380
00:19:44,733 --> 00:19:47,033
- [ELECTRICITY CRACKING]
- [LAWIN] You sure are tough.

381
00:19:47,133 --> 00:19:49,900
You went through
so many challenges,

382
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,067
- but you survived it all.
- [GABO SCREAMING IN PAIN]

383
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:57,033
[UWAK]
We thought you wouldn't last.

384
00:19:59,133 --> 00:20:02,700
[PAPANG]
But we saw your skill.

385
00:20:02,833 --> 00:20:04,567
[GABO SCREAMING]

386
00:20:04,667 --> 00:20:06,467
[PAPANG] Strength, grit...

387
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:12,133
[MEN SHOUTING]

388
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:16,967
[PAPANG]
You aren't just tough, Gabo.

389
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:20,567
You also have the conviction
to stand by your principles.

390
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,933
<i>Gabo, tonight's your chance
to escape.</i>

391
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:29,267
<i> Gabo, here's the key.</i>

392
00:20:29,367 --> 00:20:33,567
<i>Once everyone's asleep,
crawl your way out.</i>

393
00:20:33,667 --> 00:20:35,233
<i> You have to escape now.</i>

394
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:38,500
<i>Otherwise, you won't make it
till sunrise in here.</i>

395
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:45,333
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

396
00:20:46,033 --> 00:20:48,133
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

397
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:53,467
[GABO] I won't escape.

398
00:20:53,567 --> 00:20:55,167
<i> I'll stay and stand by...</i>

399
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,667
<i> ...the truth.</i>

400
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:05,500
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

401
00:21:07,567 --> 00:21:09,033
[GABO] Do you mean to say...

402
00:21:10,067 --> 00:21:14,200
...you were behind all of that?

403
00:21:14,333 --> 00:21:21,233
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

404
00:21:25,267 --> 00:21:27,167
You ****** with me!

405
00:21:30,067 --> 00:21:31,700
You should've just been upfront!

406
00:21:32,433 --> 00:21:35,733
You could've faced me
man to man!

407
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:40,867
Gabo, don't forget that Anino
gave you your freedom back.

408
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:42,867
[PAPANG] I've tested Gabo.

409
00:21:43,067 --> 00:21:48,267
<i>No one else is more suited
to join Anino.</i>

410
00:21:48,433 --> 00:21:49,567
<i> Copy, Pops.</i>

411
00:21:49,733 --> 00:21:51,567
<i>I hope you're betting
on the right person now.</i>

412
00:21:51,733 --> 00:21:54,400
<i>I can already see it.
He won't let me down.</i>

413
00:21:54,533 --> 00:21:57,500
[PAPANG] You think it's easy
to get paroled?

414
00:21:58,267 --> 00:22:00,267
Your case was hopeless, boy.

415
00:22:00,433 --> 00:22:02,200
You were up against
a politician.

416
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:04,900
And if they wanted you
to rot in jail,

417
00:22:05,033 --> 00:22:06,400
they could've made it happen.

418
00:22:07,533 --> 00:22:11,733
But Anino made the arrangements
for your release.

419
00:22:11,867 --> 00:22:15,233
Gabo, I'm aware of your case.

420
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,300
You're also a victim
of the system.

421
00:22:17,467 --> 00:22:22,100
And I believe that will push you
to work with us.

422
00:22:22,267 --> 00:22:29,200
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

423
00:22:32,233 --> 00:22:34,467
[OMENG]
Gabo, Anino needs you

424
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:38,300
to act as their hands
in taking down criminals.

425
00:22:38,433 --> 00:22:42,733
Gabo, Anino pays well
for every mission you complete.

426
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,533
Nothing stays hidden from us,
Gabo.

427
00:22:44,633 --> 00:22:46,300
We know exactly what
you've been going through

428
00:22:46,433 --> 00:22:49,133
ever since you got out
of prison.

429
00:22:49,300 --> 00:22:52,133
You tried to turn your life
around, didn't you?

430
00:22:52,267 --> 00:22:55,633
But you couldn't land
any decent job at all.

431
00:22:55,767 --> 00:22:59,167
And now your father's in
the hospital, isn't that right?

432
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:02,667
And you need money
for his treatment, don't you?

433
00:23:04,767 --> 00:23:07,667
Macaraig almost beat me to
death back inside that prison.

434
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:09,500
Turns out he was
just playing me.

435
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:12,333
Set me up good.

436
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,267
Yeah, I need cash.

437
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,300
I need work.

438
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,333
But not like this.

439
00:23:23,333 --> 00:23:25,133
Hold on.

440
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:26,767
Leave us alone for a moment.

441
00:23:26,867 --> 00:23:33,633
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

442
00:23:36,467 --> 00:23:37,600
I'm sorry, Gabo,

443
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:41,600
we didn't mean to keep
the truth from you at first.

444
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:48,267
But it's all part of screening
new members into Anino.

445
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:49,367
Tatang...

446
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:52,033
I want to change.

447
00:23:52,167 --> 00:23:54,700
This work
will change everything,

448
00:23:56,100 --> 00:24:01,733
for you, and it'll lift up
your whole family too.

449
00:24:01,867 --> 00:24:05,333
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

450
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:10,367
One hundred thousand
per mission, Gabo.

451
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:16,300
One hundred thousand
to join Anino fully.

452
00:24:16,433 --> 00:24:23,167
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

453
00:24:23,333 --> 00:24:25,633
Let me think about it.

454
00:24:25,733 --> 00:24:32,467
[MUSIC BECOMES DRAMATIC]

455
00:24:42,300 --> 00:24:43,900
<i> Gabo, how's your father doing?</i>

456
00:24:44,033 --> 00:24:45,333
<i> He's not doing well at all.</i>

457
00:24:45,433 --> 00:24:48,167
<i>Everything's gone wrong for
him, lost his mother already,</i>

458
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:50,233
<i>and now his father
gets shot like this.</i>

459
00:24:50,367 --> 00:24:52,433
<i>That was pure police brutality
what you did there!</i>

460
00:24:52,567 --> 00:24:55,233
<i>There was no police brutality
happening here!</i>

461
00:24:55,367 --> 00:24:56,667
- [OVERLAPPING SHOUTS]
<i> - What?!</i>

462
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,067
<i> He needs surgery right away.</i>

463
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,767
<i> But we have no money.</i>

464
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:05,200
I won't survive it if Rudy dies.

465
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:09,067
<i>I thought for sure
I was finally free...</i>

466
00:25:09,233 --> 00:25:11,200
<i> But turns out my freedom...</i>

467
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:14,967
...came with a heavy price tag.

468
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:17,867
<i> By opening this file,</i>

469
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,800
<i>you confirm you accept
and take on this mission.</i>

470
00:25:20,933 --> 00:25:24,100
<i>Our intel confirms we can
take down the syndicate</i>

471
00:25:24,233 --> 00:25:25,433
<i>involved in
the gold smuggling case.</i>

472
00:25:25,567 --> 00:25:29,733
<i>The man shown
in this photo is Victor Zafra.</i>

473
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,367
<i> He goes by the alias "Tiger."</i>

474
00:25:31,467 --> 00:25:33,900
<i>- Whoo!
- Go on, finish him off!</i>

475
00:25:34,067 --> 00:25:35,967
<i>He's the alleged leader
of the illegal gold mining.</i>

476
00:25:36,133 --> 00:25:37,300
<i> That's enough!</i>

477
00:25:37,433 --> 00:25:40,233
<i>Tiger is huge game,
we absolutely cannot fail.</i>

478
00:25:40,367 --> 00:25:41,767
<i> Your mission, Gabo,</i>

479
00:25:41,933 --> 00:25:46,233
it to bring Victor Zafra to us,
<i> dead or alive.</i>

480
00:25:46,367 --> 00:25:47,400
<i> This is our mission.</i>

481
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,567
<i> Failure is not an option.</i>
